# Appended to every node's /etc/hosts by `make setup-k8s-offline`, inside a
# marked block it rewrites rather than duplicates.
#
# Point k8s_hosts_file at this file in the inventory once you have copied it to
# sys/hosts and filled it in. Leave k8s_hosts_file unset and the step is skipped
# without a word, so an entry a cluster needs -- the controlPlaneEndpoint name
# above all -- is worth adding BEFORE node prep rather than after.

# The control-plane endpoint, which must resolve on every node.
10.0.0.10   cluster-control-plane
10.0.0.10   cluster-control-plane.lan

# Any other name the nodes have to resolve without DNS.
10.0.0.20   node-1
10.0.0.21   node-2
